## Notes

- AC-1's "the module imports nothing from `src/worker/` or `src/app/`" clause is asserted at compile time only (the plan's own Level 1 `tsc -b` project-reference boundary and Level 3 `grep -nE '\.\./(worker|app)'` check), not inside `test/recurrence.test.ts`: that file loads in the `worker` Vitest project, which runs inside workerd via `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` and has no `node:fs` (confirmed against this repo's own `vitest.config.ts`, which routes its two file-reading suites into a separate `docs`/plain-Node project for exactly that reason). Only AC-1's clock-free behavioural half (`vi.setSystemTime` two instants a year apart) is asserted in the suite.
- AC-5's yearly worked example (`{ freq: "yearly", dtstart: "2028-02-29" }` → `2028-02-29, 2029-02-28, 2030-02-28, 2031-02-28, 2032-02-29`) is encoded as written in the PRD and the plan **as amended on 2026-09-23**: the originally approved text skipped `2031-02-28`, the test-writer encoded that verbatim rather than repairing it silently, and the owner confirmed the correction before any production code existed, via chained `nextOccurrence(rule, { after: <previous> })` calls (an `expandOccurrences` call spanning the same 4+ year range would itself trip AC-9's 366-day guard). The sequence as stated skips a `2031-02-28` value a naive same-day-of-year stepping would otherwise produce; this is encoded faithfully rather than "corrected," per the mandate to derive tests from the PRD's literal Given/When/Then and let any real inconsistency surface as a RED result for the Implementer/reviewer to resolve, not something for the test-writer to silently reinterpret.

